B.Yg=s(["Room starts the year you turn 18 (since 2009) and never expires \u2014 unused room carries forward forever.","The 2025 and 2026 limit is $7,000/year.","Withdrawals are tax-free and are added back to your room the FOLLOWING January 1.","Over-contributing costs a 1%-per-month penalty on the excess \u2014 the number one TFSA mistake."],t.s)
B.Sc=new A.cY("TFSA limits & rules","2026","CRA")
B.Yn=s([B.Sc],t.C)
B.RT=new A.k2("tfsa","tfsa_room","TFSA, explained","A Tax-Free Savings Account lets your savings grow \u2014 and come out \u2014 completely tax-free.",B.Yg,B.Yn)
B.Ws=s(["Contributions are deductible \u2014 they reduce your taxable income at your marginal rate.","Room is 18% of your prior-year earned income up to an annual max, plus any carry-forward.","The deadline to contribute for a tax year is ~March 1 of the next year.","You can borrow from it tax-free for a first home (HBP) or schooling (LLP), with repayment rules.","Over-contributing beyond a $2,000 lifetime buffer triggers a 1%/month penalty."],t.s)
B.S6=new A.cY("RRSP deduction limit & deadline","2026","CRA")
B.VB=s([B.S6],t.C)
B.RX=new A.k2("rrsp","rrsp_room","RRSP, explained","A Registered Retirement Savings Plan lowers your tax bill now and defers tax until you withdraw (ideally in retirement at a lower rate).",B.Ws,B.VB)
B.Wt=s(["Contribute up to $8,000/year, $40,000 lifetime.","Contributions reduce your taxable income (like an RRSP).","Withdrawals for a qualifying first home are completely tax-free (like a TFSA).","Unused annual room carries forward up to $8,000.","You must be a first-time home buyer to open one; the account has a 15-year limit."],t.s)
B.Sb=new A.cY("FHSA limits & rules","2025","CRA")
B.Ur=s([B.Sb],t.C)
B.RR=new A.k2("fhsa","fhsa","FHSA, explained","The First Home Savings Account is the best of both worlds for a first home: deductible like an RRSP AND tax-free on withdrawal like a TFSA.",B.Wt,B.Ur)
B.VQ=s(["Amount is based on your adjusted family net income (AFNI) and your kids\u2019 ages.","Maximum (Jul 2025\u2013Jun 2026): $7,997/yr under 6, $6,748/yr ages 6\u201317.","It is recalculated every July from your prior-year tax return \u2014 so file on time, every year.","Higher family income gradually reduces the amount; it is never taxed."],t.s)
B.Sa=new A.cY("CCB amounts & formula","Jul 2025\u2013Jun 2026","CRA")
B.WK=s([B.Sa],t.C)
B.RQ=new A.k2("ccb","ccb","Canada Child Benefit, explained","A tax-free monthly payment to help with the cost of raising children under 18.",B.VQ,B.WK)
B.Xp=s(["Starts at age 65.","For 2025, OAS is reduced by 15\xa2 for every dollar of net income over $93,454.","It\u2019s fully clawed back around $151,668 (ages 65\u201374) / $157,490 (75+).","Splitting income with a spouse or using a TFSA (which doesn\u2019t count toward the threshold) can reduce the clawback."],t.s)
B.S9=new A.cY("OAS recovery tax","2025","Service Canada")
B.WB=s([B.S9],t.C)
B.RW=new A.k2("oas","oas","OAS clawback, explained","Old Age Security is reduced (\u201crecovered\u201d) once your income passes a threshold \u2014 the OAS recovery tax.",B.Xp,B.WB)
B.VF=s(["Principal is guaranteed \u2014 you can\u2019t lose it.","Interest is fully taxable each year UNLESS the GIC is held inside a TFSA, RRSP, or FHSA.","Your money is usually locked until maturity (cashable GICs are the exception).","At maturity, decide deliberately: reinvest, or move the cash into a tax-shelter with room."],t.s)
B.S8=new A.cY("GIC basics","\u2014","CRA")
B.XM=s([B.S8],t.C)
B.RV=new A.k2("gic","gic","GICs, explained","A Guaranteed Investment Certificate locks in your money for a set term in exchange for a guaranteed interest rate.",B.VF,B.XM)
B.WT=s(["Canada\u2019s tax is progressive: each bracket of income is taxed at its own rate.","A deduction (RRSP, FHSA) saves you tax at your marginal rate \u2014 so it\u2019s worth more the higher your income.","Example: at a 30% marginal rate, a $5,000 RRSP contribution cuts your tax by about $1,500."],t.s)
B.S7=new A.cY("Federal + provincial brackets","2025","CRA")
B.Ys=s([B.S7],t.C)
B.RY=new A.k2("marginal_rate",null,"What is your marginal tax rate?","The tax rate on your NEXT dollar of income \u2014 combined federal + provincial. It\u2019s higher than your average rate.",B.WT,B.Ys)
B.Yf=s(["TFSA: room since age 18 (2009+), unused carries forward forever, withdrawals come back next year.","RRSP: 18% of prior-year income up to a max, plus carry-forward; from your CRA Notice of Assessment.","FHSA: $8,000/year up to $40,000 lifetime.","Go over and the CRA charges a 1%/month penalty \u2014 track it."],t.s)
B.S4=new A.cY("Contribution limits","2026","CRA")
B.VX=s([B.S4],t.C)
B.RU=new A.k2("contribution_room",null,"What is contribution room?","The most you\u2019re allowed to put into a registered account. Each account tracks it differently.",B.Yf,B.VX)
B.WS=s(["RRSP wins when your tax rate now is HIGHER than it will be when you withdraw (you deduct high, withdraw low).","TFSA wins for flexibility, lower-income years, or to avoid pushing up income-tested benefits (OAS, CCB).","Saving for a first home? The FHSA usually beats both.","You don\u2019t have to choose one forever \u2014 it can change year to year."],t.s)
B.S3=new A.cY("General guidance","\u2014","CRA")
B.X4=s([B.S3],t.C)
B.RS=new A.k2("rrsp_vs_tfsa",null,"RRSP or TFSA \u2014 which first?","A rule of thumb based on your tax rate now versus in retirement.",B.WS,B.X4)
B.Yo=s(["It\u2019s both spouses\u2019/partners\u2019 net incomes combined, with a few adjustments.","Lowering it (e.g. via RRSP/FHSA deductions) can INCREASE benefits like the CCB.","It\u2019s taken from your filed tax returns \u2014 another reason to file on time."],t.s)
B.S5=new A.cY("AFNI definition","\u2014","CRA")
B.W0=s([B.S5],t.C)
B.RP=new A.k2("afni",null,"What is adjusted family net income (AFNI)?","The income figure the CRA uses to size income-tested benefits like the Canada Child Benefit.",B.Yo,B.W0)
